>> title: Chili con Carne, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, chiles, texas, one-pot, stew, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: chili-con-carne
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: chili, bowl of red, Texas red, chili no beans, instant pot chili, pressure cooker chili con carne
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 35 min
>> step.2: brown 12 min, in two batches
>> step.3: soften
>> step.4: bloom the chile off the heat
>> step.5: 35 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
>> step.6: thicken with masa, lid off

Two things scorch on a sealed base and neither can be seen through the lid: ground chile, and tomato stirred down to the bottom. Bloom the chile with the pot switched off, and pour the tomatoes over the top without stirring them in.

Brown @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1/2-in dice), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~brown{12%min}, in two batches.

Soften @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced) with @&(~1)browned beef{}.

Bloom @ancho chile powder{1/4%cup}(30 g; pure ground chile, not a chili-powder blend), @ground cumin{1%Tbs}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} in @&(~1)pot{} with the heat switched off, then scrape the base until nothing is stuck to it.

Pressure cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @crushed tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g; poured over, not stirred down), @cider vinegar{1%Tbs}, lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{12%min}, then ~pressure cook{35%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}. Fine dice under pressure comes out shreddable, which in a bowl of red is not a fault.

Thicken @&(~1)chili{} with @masa harina{2%Tbs}(20 g; slaked in a little water) on sauté for ~thicken{8%min}, lid off.
